# Kisan Bazar — Frontend

## File Structure
```
frontend/
├── index.html        ← Single entry point (open this in browser)
├── css/
│   └── style.css     ← All styles (mobile-first, earthy theme)
└── js/
    └── app.js        ← All logic (navigation, CRUD, search, modal)
```

## How to Test on Mobile
1. Open `index.html` directly in your mobile browser (Chrome/Firefox).
2. All data is saved to **localStorage** — no backend needed yet.
3. Later, replace `localStorage` calls in `app.js` with `fetch()` API calls.

## Pages
- **Home** — Role selection (Farmer / Buyer)
- **Farmer Panel** — Add crop listings, view & delete own listings
- **Buyer Panel** — Browse all crops, search, filter by category, contact farmer

## Backend Integration (Later)
When your Flask/Node backend is ready:
- `addCrop()` → POST `/api/crops`
- `renderFarmerListings()` → GET `/api/crops`
- `deleteCrop(id)` → DELETE `/api/crops/:id`
